29. Security Considerations

Because the project was intended as a cybersecurity portfolio, screenshots and configuration files should be reviewed before being published.

Sensitive information such as:

Public IP addresses;
Personal usernames;
Hostnames containing personal information;
MAC addresses;
Internal infrastructure details;
Authentication credentials;
API keys;
Passwords;

should not be exposed unnecessarily.

For a portfolio project, replacing sensitive information with placeholders such as:

192.168.X.X
HOSTNAME
USER
REDACTED

is preferable when the information is not necessary to demonstrate the technical result.

