31. Conclusion

This project provided a practical implementation of a SOC/SIEM laboratory using Wazuh.

The implementation started with the deployment of Ubuntu Server 24.04 and the installation of the Wazuh infrastructure. Windows 10 and Kali Linux were subsequently configured as monitored endpoints.

The environment was then enhanced with Sysmon on Windows and Auditd on Kali Linux, providing additional security telemetry for investigation.

Additional Wazuh capabilities, including File Integrity Monitoring, vulnerability detection, inventory, and MITRE ATT&CK mapping, were also explored.

Finally, controlled security activities were performed using Kali Linux, including Nmap-based reconnaissance, allowing the monitoring pipeline to be validated from the generation of an event to its visualization and investigation in the Wazuh Dashboard.

The final laboratory therefore demonstrates the fundamental workflow of a defensive security operation:

Collect → Detect → Alert → Investigate → Analyze → Respond

This project provided practical experience with technologies and concepts commonly associated with SOC Analyst, Blue Team, SIEM, Endpoint Detection, Security Monitoring, Incident Investigation, and Threat Detection roles.
